# The wave prices every non-solid cell the same, so a plan to a smell waypoint or a far frontier runs straight through unknown ground as if it were open floor, and the agent is led into walls and dead ends it could not see. Making the step cost depend on KNOWLEDGE (an extra discount for each unknown cell crossed, none on known-free floor) makes the plan prefer routes over ground it has seen, and it weighs a target behind unexplored terrain as the gamble it is, without adding any new source or changing the read-out.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel bad
channel here
channel value
channel dark
channel injection
channel wave
channel trail

rule track:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.97 * trail)

rule darkness:
  when 1
  set dark = 0.5 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid) + 0.5 * avg8(dark)

rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(where(scent + thing < 0.05, 0, source), thing * (1 - bad), where(scent + thing < 0.05, source, 0) * (0.3 + 2.0 * dark)) / (1 + 0.5 * sum8(solid))

# a step costs more where the ground is not known to be free: a plan through unknown land may hit a wall
rule plan:
  when 1
  set wave = max(injection, (1 - 0.08 * (1 - free)) * max(0.94 * max4(wave), 0.916214 * max8(wave))) * (1 - solid * (1 - leak))

rule read:
  when 1
  set value = wave * (1 - 0.4 * trail)
